WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.161
In this video, we'll introduce how sponsored display can help drive traffic to your detail pages

00:00:05.161 --> 00:00:10.000
and how you can set up your own sponsored display campaigns in the Advertising Console.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.455
Sponsored display allows you to create display ads that can appear when shoppers browse, research,

00:00:15.455 --> 00:00:18.000
or buy products in the Amazon store.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.833
Sponsored display ads can appear on the Amazon homepage, product detail pages, shopping results,

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:28.000
Twitch, as well as other sites where shoppers spend time.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
These ads can link shoppers directly to your product detail pages to learn more about your brand.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.571
Sponsored display ads are automatically generated from product detail pages and include product

00:00:39.571 --> 00:00:43.000
features like price and star rating alongside images.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.000
This allows you to quickly set up display ads to reach shoppers in new placements.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Now let's learn how to get started with your first sponsored display campaign.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
First, define your campaign goals.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.600
Before you start, consider the goals of your campaign.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:03.200
Sponsored display can help you achieve a variety of advertising goals, like awareness, consideration,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.000
and purchase.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Depending on your goal, you may want to evaluate different metrics to assess your campaign's performance.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.600
Second, create a campaign.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:17.600
Now that you've identified your goals, sign into your Advertising Console account and click Create

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.000
Campaign.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.739
Then choose Sponsored Display and click Continue.

00:01:20.739 --> 00:01:22.696
Third, choose your campaign settings.

00:01:22.696 --> 00:01:27.000
Choose a campaign name that is easy to identify and remember.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Note that this campaign name is only visible to you.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Next, enter the start and end dates for your campaign.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Remember, it's recommended to create your campaign with no end date so it can run year-round unless

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.000
you have a specific seasonal goal.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.667
Finally, set your daily budget.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:46.333
Fourth, create an ad group and choose your ad group settings.

00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:52.667
Ad groups are groups of ads within a campaign that share the same creative type or set of targeting

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.000
tactics.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.208
The first ad group is created when you create a campaign.

00:01:56.208 --> 00:02:00.000
You can add more ad groups to the campaign after you've saved it.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.182
Give your ad group a name that is descriptive and meaningful to you based on the products that you

00:02:05.182 --> 00:02:06.000
want to advertise.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.944
Fifth, customize your bidding strategies.

00:02:07.944 --> 00:02:13.000
Choose a bidding strategy that lets Amazon optimize your bids against specific metrics.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.793
You can choose to optimize for reach, page visits, or conversions.

00:02:16.793 --> 00:02:22.310
Bids automatically adjust based on relevance while still allowing you to change your bid or pause

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.000
your campaign.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.562
Sixth, select an ad format.

00:02:24.562 --> 00:02:29.250
Ad formats can help you create an ad based on what you want to promote.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.000
Sponsored display gives you access to two ad formats, image and video.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.333
The image ad format lets you promote unique collections of products or existing stores, while the

00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:41.000
video format lets you feature a single product.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.310
The image creative for your campaign is automatically generated from the product detail page.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:52.000
You can customize the default image creative with your brand logo, headline, and lifestyle imagery.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.565
To create a sponsored display campaign with video, you'll need to upload an existing video asset

00:02:57.565 --> 00:03:00.000
that features a single product or brand.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.440
Seventh, choose your products.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:07.200
We recommend adding 10 or more retail ready products to ensure your audiences see products that

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.000
are ready to be advertised.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.944
Eighth, choose your targeting tactic.

00:03:10.944 --> 00:03:16.000
Sponsored display gives you the option to choose between contextual targeting and audiences.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.913
Note that only one targeting type per campaign is supported.

00:03:19.913 --> 00:03:25.000
Contextual targeting lets you choose specific products or categories to target your ads.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.053
You can show ads to shoppers who are currently visiting products and categories that you select

00:03:30.053 --> 00:03:31.000
and similar products.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:36.294
With different selected targets, you can choose to reach new audiences across diverse contexts on

00:03:36.294 --> 00:03:42.294
their shopping and entertainment on Amazon and wherever they spend time, as well as on Amazon product

00:03:42.294 --> 00:03:43.000
detail pages.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.000
Audiences let you choose which audiences you want to see your ads.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.250
You can reach relevant audiences through their shopping and entertainment journey inside and outside

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.000
the Amazon store using shopping and streaming signals from Amazon.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.037
You have the option to combine multiple audiences in a single campaign, which can create a broader

00:04:01.037 --> 00:04:04.000
audience for your ads while removing the risk of overlap.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Ninth, provide your targeting details.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:11.600
Pending your targeting tactic selection, your final step will be to provide different targeting

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.000
details.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:17.455
If you choose contextual targeting as your targeting tactic, here you can select categories, products,

00:04:17.455 --> 00:04:20.000
brands, or features related to your product.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:26.261
If you choose audiences as your targeting tactic, here you can further refine audiences by brand,

00:04:26.261 --> 00:04:29.000
price range, star rating, and shipping eligibility.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:34.727
Once you complete these steps, you're ready to launch your first sponsored display campaign.

00:04:34.727 --> 00:04:36.364
Ready to get started?

00:04:36.364 --> 00:04:37.182
Visit ads.

00:04:37.182 --> 00:04:37.591
amazon.

00:04:37.591 --> 00:04:38.000
com.
